    "kind": "behavior",
    "description": "S1 now has immediate action-history refresh with independent unread/New/action indicators and retained drafts; S3 includes protected later selection when an old detail read finishes. Existing revision-aware reads and no-implicit-launch behavior remain. Public source publication replaces personal operator details with installation-neutral documentation, omits private evidence/history, and retains the same scope of existing runtime assertions; hosted verification uses fixtures only.",
    "implementation": "Inspected ItemDetail.mutate/read version and alive/selected-id guards plus Factory.action refresh behavior. Successful selected item actions reread detail/history; a late older response cannot replace another selected item, and unchanged displayed revision does not trigger another consuming read. Public source publication replaces personal operator details with installation-neutral documentation, omits private evidence/history, and retains the same scope of existing runtime assertions; hosted verification uses fixtures only.",
    "tests": "Read UI-ITEM-ACTIONS assertions for one visible action row, independent unread/New flags, retained link/priority drafts and one read/no launch, plus UI-DETAIL-SELECTION gated response assertions. Filter combinations, failed reads, revision/remount variants and the complete installed-host matrix remain gaps. Public source publication replaces personal operator details with installation-neutral documentation, omits private evidence/history, and retains the same scope of existing runtime assertions; hosted verification uses fixtures only."
